      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the person in <Picture 1>. Reference role: identity, face, hair, and outfit anchor. Preserve facial features, hairstyle, build, and clothing accurately.\n<Subject 2> is the environment in <Picture 2> (or the background of <Picture 1> if <Picture 2> is disconnected). Reference role: location, lighting, and atmosphere anchor.\n<Video 1> is the motion and camera reference clip only. Do NOT copy the person, face, outfit, or background from <Video 1>.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] A five-second cinematic shot where <Subject 1> from <Picture 1> performs the exact body movement, timing, and camera choreography of <Video 1> inside <Subject 2>.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - face, hair, clothing, and identity from <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - environment, lighting, and palette from <Picture 2>.\n<Video 1> (motion & camera): attribute_transfer - transfer the body motion, pacing, gesture rhythm, and camera movement from <Video 1>; treat the appearance and setting of <Video 1> as weak_reference and discard them completely.\nNo audio reference is used in this generation.\n\ndetailed_description:\nNatural cinematic photography with realistic skin texture, consistent lighting, and smooth motion.\n\n[Shot 1] Inside <Subject 2>, <Subject 1> performs the exact movement sequence and pacing from <Video 1>, matching the body motion, head turns, and camera choreography cleanly while keeping <Subject 1>'s exact face, outfit, and the environment of <Subject 2> throughout the entire five-second shot.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nNatural ambient room tone and subtle footsteps/clothing movement synced to <Subject 1>'s motion.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the person in <Picture 1>. Reference role: identity, face, hair, and outfit anchor. Preserve facial features, hairstyle, build, and clothing accurately.\n<Subject 2> is the environment in <Picture 2> (or the background of <Picture 1> if <Picture 2> is disconnected). Reference role: location, lighting, and atmosphere anchor.\n<Video 1> is the motion and camera reference clip only. Do NOT copy the person, face, outfit, or background from <Video 1>.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] A five-second cinematic shot where <Subject 1> from <Picture 1> performs the exact body movement, timing, and camera choreography of <Video 1> inside <Subject 2>.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - face, hair, clothing, and identity from <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - environment, lighting, and palette from <Picture 2>.\n<Video 1> (motion & camera): attribute_transfer - transfer the body motion, pacing, gesture rhythm, and camera movement from <Video 1>; treat the appearance and setting of <Video 1> as weak_reference and discard them completely.\nNo audio reference is used in this generation.\n\ndetailed_description:\nNatural cinematic photography with realistic skin texture, consistent lighting, and smooth motion.\n\n[Shot 1] Inside <Subject 2>, <Subject 1> performs the exact movement sequence and pacing from <Video 1>, matching the body motion, head turns, and camera choreography cleanly while keeping <Subject 1>'s exact face, outfit, and the environment of <Subject 2> throughout the entire five-second shot.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nNatural ambient room tone and subtle footsteps/clothing movement synced to <Subject 1>'s motion.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
